        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Geotechnical Engineering - Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The most widely used in-situ test in the world:\n- Drop 140-lb hammer 30 inches onto split-spoon sampler\n- Count blows for last 12 inches of 18-inch drive = N-value\n- N-value correlates with density (sands), consistency (clays), bearing capacity, liquefaction potential\n- Energy correction: N60 (corrected to 60% efficiency); overburden correction: (N1)60"
    },
