        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Geotechnical Engineering - Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Increasingly preferred for soft soils:\n- Continuous electronic log of tip resistance qc and sleeve friction fs\n- No sample but continuous stratigraphic profile\n- Corrections: qt (pore pressure correction for thin tip); Rf = fs/qc (friction ratio)\n- Rf ~ 0.5-1% = clean sand; Rf ~ 4-7% = clay\n- CPTu adds pore pressure measurement u2 — resolves fine-grained vs. coarse"
    },
